# LegendList 3.7.1 for the native chat timeline (docs/agent-stream-disclosure.md).
# Upstream: https://github.com/LegendApp/legend-list/issues/593 covers every change below.
# react-native.js and react-native.mjs carry the same hunks; each has a "Paseo patch" comment.
#
# 1. getEstimatedItemSize (react-native.d.ts, getItemSize, LegendListInner props): a per-item
#    estimate for an unmeasured row wins over the running average for its type.
# 2. MVCP anchor lock on native (canRestoreAnchorLock, resolveAnchorLock, updateAnchorLock,
#    prepareMVCP): upstream enables it on web only. On native the lock ends when its row leaves
#    the view or shouldRestorePosition rejects it, instead of after 300 ms.
# 3. Preserved initial end only with maintainScrollAtEnd (finishScrollTo,
#    finishBootstrapInitialScrollWithoutScroll): otherwise every data change re-arms the initial
#    scroll to the end.
# 4. Silent initial scroll retry in one task (checkFinishedScrollFallback): the nudge and the return
#    to the target go out together, so Android does not reveal 1 dp short of the end.
# 5. Layout noise against the floored known size (isNativeLayoutNoise, updateOneItemSize): a
#    one-pixel snap change is not a resize.
# 6. Content height from React state on the New Architecture (useContentSize, ContainersLayer):
#    the Animated height mounts the estimated layout for a frame.
# 7. Header and footer revealed with the rows (RevealedLayoutView, ListComponent).
# 8. Top-padding shrink hold on iOS only (setPaddingTop): Android paints the held height as blank
#    space at the end.
# 9. Rows cut off at the top count as in view, and so does the row just past the end of the
#    viewport (getIdsInVisibleRange): they follow the fully visible rows in idsInView, so a
#    disclosure hold on a row whose top is above the viewport still anchors on that row instead
#    of the row below it, and a hold on the row below a bottom-edge trigger anchors even when
#    that row starts below the viewport.
# 10. A size change keeps only a row shouldRestorePosition accepts in place (prepareMVCP), as a
#    data change already does, so a disclosure that only grows (a todo card) holds the cut-off
#    row instead of the first row in view.
# 11. A 0 x 0 measurement is not a size (updateItemSizesBatch): rows of a hidden retained tab
#    (display: none) still render and measure 0 x 0. Recording it collapsed the row, and a row
#    whose frame was unchanged when the tab showed again got no layout event to correct it.
# 12. No Android clamp prediction for a size change (prepareMVCP): upstream measures the adjustment
#    of a shrink past the end from the new end, assuming the scroll view clamped first. The app's
#    scroll view clamps after the adjustment on both platforms (modules/paseo-scroll), so a
#    bottom-edge disclosure collapsing near the end landed at the end instead of in place.
#
# Upgrading: drop each hunk whose fix the new version ships, regenerate with
# `npx patch-package @legendapp/list`, and copy this header back on top.
